-- The learned statistic keyed on the object the substrate actually stores.
-- A piece-square cell is a projection (a dot product over every arrival path);
-- a move is a lookup. 7,797 distinct tier-2 move entities cover 1.6M games, so
-- this folds unbounded testimony into a small bounded table. No replay: ordered
-- move ids are the record and ply parity is the mover.
-- p_games is REQUIRED to be bounded by default. The first cut shipped DEFAULT 0
-- (whole corpus), which folds ~135M trajectory constituents through SPI in one
-- call and does not return on a 1.6M-game corpus -- a query surface must not have
-- a hang as its default. This is a PASS, not a lookup: the statistic it produces
-- is 7,797 bounded rows and belongs materialized in laplace.consensus, read O(1)
-- thereafter, which is exactly what chess.moves already reads and what the rated
-- MOVE web was designed to hold. Materializing it is the follow-up; until then
-- callers must state how much testimony they are willing to pay for.
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS chess.learned_moves(integer);
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION chess.learned_moves(p_games integer DEFAULT 20000)
    RETURNS TABLE(move_id bytea, plays bigint, mover_score double precision)
    LANGUAGE C STABLE PARALLEL SAFE
    AS 'MODULE_PATHNAME', 'pg_laplace_chess_learned_moves';
